From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: danieljesus <danieljesus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:33:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [stream] include <cstdlib> for std::abort

stream.h calls std::abort() but relied on another header to declare it.
libc++ from LLVM 23 (Homebrew clang 23.1.6) no longer brings <cstdlib> in
through the headers it includes, so sirit fails to build there without an
-include cstdlib workaround.
---
 src/stream.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/stream.h b/src/stream.h
index 31c2680..f7cf0df 100644
--- a/src/stream.h
+++ b/src/stream.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <cassert>
 #include <concepts>
 #include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <functional>
 #include <string_view>
 #include <unordered_map>
